      "text": "QUANTIZATION",
      "fontSize": 226.86956521739123,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "QUANTIZATION",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "I7m7nP249iGtDFyRFUJ8A",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12925.532851097643,
      "y": 2123.4840718543433,
      "width": 326.62811279296875,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "z7TDSIQOcrmSiEu4b3YGb",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1198117478,
      "version": 576,
      "versionNonce": 1812134210,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is Quantization",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is Quantization",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wQ2_Q6CPgFVlY7Ie2DAm4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13287.032851097643,
      "y": 2187.584071854343,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "z7TDSIQOcrmSiEu4b3YGb",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1955501478,
      "version": 848,
      "versionNonce": 79016926,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quantization is a model compression technique that converts the weights and activations within an LLM\nfrom a high-precision data representation to a lower-precision data representation\n\n                            data type with more info --> data type with less info",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quantization is a model compression technique that converts the weights and activations within an LLM from a high-precision data representation to a lower-precision data representation\n\n                            data type with more info --> data type with less info",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "B5jUWsrZIC4SQyMH-t6nk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13235.961850163996,
      "y": 3833.3169589634626,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "_PGi3pEmSD9oauhnbZml8",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2126049510,
      "version": 1527,
      "versionNonce": 295076098,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-\ndemand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit amnd run faster.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-demand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit amnd run faster.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BquklqXHi3debMCLZzVxw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13046.170732813738,
      "y": 3762.8836256301306,
      "width": 634.8963012695312,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "_PGi3pEmSD9oauhnbZml8",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1635116070,
      "version": 888,
      "versionNonce": 1506773022,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why using quantization -> $$$ and speed",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why using quantization -> $$$ and speed",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lJ4Lvu-UUxP6n28hu-zfY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12919.19515307512,
      "y": 11068.324965652748,
      "width": 673.164306640625,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "ToPcOopNFjmBlDgdqL4pq",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 515010406,
      "version": 1848,
      "versionNonce": 316870850,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When Quantization: Training and Inference ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When Quantization: Training and Inference ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lISR-HzW_6iR7P6zguieP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13107.163248627472,
      "y": 11142.002354158834,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "ToPcOopNFjmBlDgdqL4pq",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1924895398,
      "version": 3622,
      "versionNonce": 1294259294,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quantization can be done in 2 stages of a model:\n\nQuantized traininig\n- historically  in full precision\n- present in half precision with bfloat16\n- recent llm (deepseekR1 and llama4) trained on float8 but no public procedure\n\nInference is more resilient in loss in precision.\n\nPost-training dynamic quantization\n- load the trained model and convert model weights and activations ahead of time\n- rescale activations on the fly, just before running the computation\n- the scale factor is computed dynamically, which is simple, more flexible but has some overhead\n\nPost-training static quantization\n- load the trained model and convert model weights and activations ahead of time\n- predict a calibration dataset, and use the observed distribution of activations to set the scale\nfactor\n- no overhead and lower latency, calibration may not work well for all datasets\n\nQuantization aware training\nSometimes training is done taking into account future quantization\n- train still at full precision\n- obtain higher quality models, but need to retrain which is expensive for LLM (1bit LLMs)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quantization can be done in 2 stages of a model:\n\nQuantized traininig\n- historically  in full precision\n- present in half precision with bfloat16\n- recent llm (deepseekR1 and llama4) trained on float8 but no public procedure\n\nInference is more resilient in loss in precision.\n\nPost-training dynamic quantization\n- load the trained model and convert model weights and activations ahead of time\n- rescale activations on the fly, just before running the computation\n- the scale factor is computed dynamically, which is simple, more flexible but has some overhead\n\nPost-training static quantization\n- load the trained model and convert model weights and activations ahead of time\n- predict a calibration dataset, and use the observed distribution of activations to set the scale factor\n- no overhead and lower latency, calibration may not work well for all datasets\n\nQuantization aware training\nSometimes training is done taking into account future quantization\n- train still at full precision\n- obtain higher quality models, but need to retrain which is expensive for LLM (1bit LLMs)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gqdn8_pDPzjM4NTiXUcy7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12743.909574591493,
      "y": 9927.842517634961,
      "width": 171.39605712890625,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
