    {
      "id": "5Sza_1w1wwto0TP7v6IQj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13264.642819296329,
      "y": 3179.18376503152,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g_-ijr369BUDKlUINiYO-",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 709741606,
      "version": 959,
      "versionNonce": 754138370,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A common way to  representing real numbers is through floating-point: the number of digits for\nrepresenting the integer and the fractional parts can vary. \n    - FP16 (half-precision)\n    - FP32 (full-precision)\n    - bFP16\n\nThere are three components in the floating-point representation:\n    1. The sign bit: this is the bit specifying the sign of the number.\n    2. The exponent part\n    3. The mantissa/fraction/significant",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A common way to  representing real numbers is through floating-point: the number of digits for representing the integer and the fractional parts can vary. \n    - FP16 (half-precision)\n    - FP32 (full-precision)\n    - bFP16\n\nThere are three components in the floating-point representation:\n    1. The sign bit: this is the bit specifying the sign of the number.\n    2. The exponent part\n    3. The mantissa/fraction/significant",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hMczm0hphvOY5NWM7TopL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12831.729975283662,
      "y": 5633.5083199321,
      "width": 311.54412841796875,
      "height": 41.4,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "1EIIz1ADEoG0QKGcDi__6",
        "1cRHfAFHlJ2L2jbrzde9d",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1414354790,
      "version": 1543,
      "versionNonce": 1017941022,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quantization to int8",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quantization to int8",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eoB9w0PyTsk_irADOdD31",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13147.649360058367,
      "y": 5688.196892161755,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "1EIIz1ADEoG0QKGcDi__6",
        "1cRHfAFHlJ2L2jbrzde9d",
        "2BSV0B04mK-tRxLppZJv1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bgr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 79264422,
      "version": 2601,
      "versionNonce": 457723074,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789588462877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Performing quantization to go from float32 to int8 is tricky. How do we go from [-1, 1] to [-128, 127]?\n\nThe mapping function which converts float to int is also called quantization scheme.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe range in which we are going to quantize is called clipping range. In some quantization schemes the\nfirst value is also dropped to have a symmetric interval. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Performing quantization to go from float32 to int8 is tricky. How do we go from [-1, 1] to [-128, 127]?\n\nThe mapping function which converts float to int is also called quantization scheme.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe range in which we are going to quantize is called clipping range. In some quantization schemes the first value is also dropped to have a symmetric interval. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iE1g4xVllYFKLPRgnFtFe",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": -12996.952012860162,
      "y": 5821.231161032945,
      "width": 386.66666666666674,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
